course: dictionary
lesson: 14268
title: Ordinal numbers: nineteenth
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Nineteenth» tells you a place in an order, like first, second, third, and so on. It comes after eighteenth and before twentieth, and it is written 19th.
explain: «Mia was the nineteenth runner to cross the finish line.» Nineteenth tells you Mia's place: eighteen runners came before her. Ask yourself: is this a place in a line, or an amount? Here it is a place, so nineteenth fits.
explain: Nineteenth can also name a part of something. «Cut the cake into nineteen equal pieces, and each piece is a nineteenth.» A nineteenth is one of nineteen equal parts, written 1/19.
fact: Nineteenth is an ordinal number: it tells the place or position in an order.
fact: «My birthday is on the nineteenth of May» means the 19th day of the month.
fact: A nineteenth is one of nineteen equal parts, and we write it as 1/19.
fact: «The nineteenth century» is the hundred years we call the 1800s, the time of steam trains and Queen Victoria.
exercise: «Mia was the nineteenth runner to finish.» What does nineteenth tell us? | *Her place in the race, 19th | How fast she ran | Her age | How many runners there were
exercise: Ben says, «My birthday is on the nineteenth of May.» What does nineteenth mean here? | The 19 days in May | *The 19th day of the month | The 19th month of the year | A nineteen-pound present
exercise: A pizza is cut into nineteen equal slices. What is one slice called? | Half | Nineteen | Twenty | *A nineteenth
test: «Lara finished in the nineteenth place.» Find and copy the word that shows her place. | finished | Lara | *nineteenth | place
test: Which one is written as 1/19? | *A nineteenth | Nineteenth century | Nineteen | Nineteen parts
exam: «The nineteenth century was the time of steam trains.» What does nineteenth century mean? | The nineteenth person to build a train | *The hundred years we call the 1800s | Nineteen hundred years, one after another | A very old and slow train
